<article class="env-definition" id="0DQV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DQV">Definition <span data-tag="0DQV">107.2.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0DQU" data-tag="0DQU">107.2.1</a> let $x_0 : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to \mathcal{X}$ be a morphism, where $k$ is a finite type field over $S$. A <em>versal ring to $\mathcal{X}$ at $x_0$</em> is a complete Noetherian local $S$-algebra $A$ with residue field $k$ such that there exists a versal formal object $(A, \xi _ n, f_ n)$ as in Artin's Axioms, Definition <a href="/tag/0CXJ" data-tag="0CXJ">98.12.1</a> with $\xi _1 \cong x_0$ (a $2$-isomorphism). </p>
</article>